          "title": "Potential 1NF Violation (Multi-Valued Attribute) in \"products.tags\"",
          "category": "structure",
          "severity": "MEDIUM",
          "description": "The column \"tags\" in \"products\" suggests non-atomic multi-valued items stored in a single field (e.g. comma-separated lists).",
          "evidence": "Column name pattern indicates multi-value list: \"tags\"",
          "databaseObject": "products.tags",
          "table": "products",
          "column": "tags",
          "whyItMatters": "1NF requires all attribute values to be atomic. Storing comma-separated lists prevents exact indexing, forces costly wildcard searches (LIKE \"%tag%\"), and prevents relational constraints.",
          "recommendation": "Normalize into a junction/associative table (e.g. \"products_tags\") with a foreign key to \"products\".",
          "confidence": 85,
          "risk": "MEDIUM",
          "expectedImpact": "Enables exact index lookups, clean relational queries, and simplifies reporting.",
          "suggestedFix": "-- Recommended Schema Normalization:\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \"products_tags\" (\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n  \"products_id\" INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  value VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,\n  FOREIGN KEY (\"products_id\") REFERENCES \"products\"(id)\n);",
          "status": "APPLIED",
          "safeToApplyAuto": false
