        "content": "### Dataset Table Specification: **\"Retail & E-Commerce Platform\"**\n\nBased on the authoritative dataset document, there are exactly **8 tables** in this dataset:\n\n| # | Table Name | Estimated Rows | Columns | Primary Key | Foreign Keys |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **`activity_log`** | 5 | 4 | `None` | 0 |\n| 2 | **`categories`** | 4 | 4 | `id` | 0 |\n| 3 | **`order_items`** | 7 | 6 | `id` | 2 |\n| 4 | **`orders`** | 5 | 8 | `id` | 1 |\n| 5 | **`payments`** | 5 | 8 | `id` | 1 |\n| 6 | **`products`** | 5 | 9 | `id` | 1 |\n| 7 | **`reviews`** | 4 | 6 | `id` | 2 |\n| 8 | **`users`** | 5 | 11 | `id` | 0 |\n\n**Dataset Metrics Summary:**\n- **Total Tables**: 8\n- **Total Columns**: 56\n- **Total Foreign Key Relationships**: 7\n- **Total Secondary Indexes**: 1\n- **Total Estimated Records**: 40\n- **Database Engine**: SQLITE\n\nYou can ask me to inspect the columns of any table (e.g. *\"Show columns in activity_log\"*) or generate a read-only query.",
